toolCallId":"call_43b5e9042a0a4153b220627a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"eval #6: rmse = 0.86618 (+/- 0.0598 over 9 folds) \n  features=8 views=1 time=8.88s | P0=0.86191 best_before=0.86191\n  secondary: rmse=0.8662, mae=0.5945, r2=0.6325\n  budget: 6/24 evaluations used\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790974460143},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me step back and try the simplest possible improvement - just using the original pipeline with the log transformation, but let's also check what the best result so far was and consider if we should stick with the original approach since it's performing well:\n\nLooking at the results:\n- P0 (original): 0.86191 \n- My attempts: 0.86540, 0.86620, 0.86687, 0.86461, 0.86618\n\nThe best attempt so far is 0.86461, which is slightly worse than the baseline. However, I notice that the variance in the results is quite low (±0.06), which suggests that the dataset might be quite stable and difficult to improve upon significantly.\n\nLet me try one more approach that uses a very minimal feature engineering that focuses on what we know from the correlation analysis - using the most correlated features:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d2e01de78e664e5191ba5e64","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"pipeline.py","content":"import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Log transform the target variable to handle skewness\n    y_train_log = np.log1p(y_train)  # log(1+x) to handle zeros\n    return X_train, y_train_log, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Minimal engineering - just use the most correlated features\n    # MLOGP has highest correlation with LC50 (0.652)\n    # SM1_Dz(Z) has moderate correlation (0.409)\n    # GATS1i has negative correlation (-0.396)\n    \n    # We'll keep the original features and add one interaction that makes sense\n    X_train_eng = X_train.copy()\n    X_test_eng = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Add the most strongly correlated features' interaction\n    X_train_eng['MLOGP_interaction'] = X_train['MLOGP'] * X_train['SM1_Dz(Z)']\n    X_test_eng['MLOGP_interaction'] = X_test['MLOGP'] * X_test['SM1_Dz(Z)']\n    \n    return X_train_eng, X_test_eng\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    # Invert the log transformation\n    return np.expm1(pred)  # exp(x) - 1 to invert log(1+x)"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":9610,"output":593,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10203,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790974460147,"responseId":"chatcmpl-911eb49d0e6985ac","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d2e01de78e664e5191ba5e64","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to pipeline.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790974463078},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4edfc85b33b74287adbcfde6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"tabfm-eval"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":10222,"output":25,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10247,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790974463080,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b7d12be084c57a71","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4edfc85b33b74287adbcfde6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"eval #7: rmse = 0.86250 (+/- 0.0640 over 9 folds) \n  features=7 views=1 time=8.89s | P0=0.86191 best_before=